        "timestamp": 1778599937,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Over the weekend, Paris hosted the annual Lépine competition, a moment for inventors to put the spotlight on their ideas, and which has been going for well over a century. An aquatic hoover took first prize this year, and if that sounds a little confusing, don't worry, France 24's Luke Shrago explains it all for you."
